All 15 tests pass (`15 passed in 0.02s`). The 9 failures were independent bugs across 3 modules — all fixed in `src/` only, no test files touched.

**`src/auth.py`**
- `has_permission` was case-sensitive (`"Admin"` vs `"admin"`). Now lowercases both sides before comparing.
- `is_admin_or_owner` used `and` instead of `or` — admin *and* owner were both required. Now admin alone or owner alone grants access.

**`src/inventory.py`**
- `__init__` used a shared mutable default `{}` — every instance saw the same stock dict. Switched to `None` default with a fresh copy per instance (`test_two_inventories_do_not_share_state`).
- `add` overwrote stock instead of accumulating; now adds to existing quantity.
- `reserve` raised `OutOfStock` when `qty >= available`, rejecting reservations exactly equal to available stock. Now only `qty > available` raises.

**`src/text_utils.py`**
- `slugify` didn't lowercase input and only collapsed a single `--` pair. Now lowercases and collapses all separator runs via `re.sub(r"-+", "-")`.
- `truncate` produced `max_len + 1` chars (suffix was appended on top of the full slice). Now truncates to `max_len - len(suffix)` before adding the suffix, so total length respects `max_len` while still ending in `…`.
